# Whether every member of an interval of the round-up interval is negative: xu < 0 (xu is never
# -inf, and a NaN makes it false for the empty set); the default interval_negative_1 on the meaning.
# Exact, in every rounding mode (docs/developer/design/upward.md, "Predicates and comparisons").
# Requires the rounding mode upward set by kairn::upward::Scope and the options of
# docs/concepts/upward.md (GCC and Clang -frounding-math, MSVC /fp:strict).
kernel:        upward_negative_1
rounding:      upward
input:         pair stored x = xu xn
output:        mask m
requires:      upward xu xn
ensures:       certain m lt x 0 x=xu,xn exact
min_precision: 1
source:        the upper bound compared with 0 (the listing of the round-up interval)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        unverified
domain:        extended
ieee_only:     yes
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the result is a mask, which has no non-finite value, and a comparison with NaN is false; certain states what comes out for every canonical operand
unused:        xn the upper bound alone tells: every member is at most it, and the state is empty exactly when it is a NaN

m = lt(xu, 0)
